{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "or-large-file-handling-2026-11-15",
		"name": "OpenRegister Uploads In Parts",
		"description": "REQ-LFH-002/003 through the routes (openspec/changes/large-file-handling, task 3.3).\n\nWHAT IT ASSERTS: a session for a 25 MiB file opens at 10 MiB parts (201, three end-inclusive ranges); parts 1 and 3 are stored out of order; the status then names part 2 as missing with complete false; part 2 completes the set; complete answers 201 with the file, and GET .../files lists it at the full 26214400 bytes. The file is generated in the pre-request scripts from the plan's ranges (MiB m is a 64-byte block naming m, repeated), so nothing large is stored in the repository; its SHA-256 is fixed below and checked by the server on complete.\n\nAssumes the instance's default part size (upload.partSizeBytes = 10485760); the collection does not change settings.",
